{
 "id": "gripper-finger-fdm",
 "brief": "A gripper finger in PETG, FDM, printed flat (layers along Z). It pivots on a 3 mm pin along Z at\nthe origin (3.2 mm hole, keep 2.5 mm of wall round it). A second 3.2 mm hole for the drive link\npin is at (12, -8), also along Z, with the same 2.5 mm wall. The fingertip is a flat gripping\npad: x = 60 to 70, y = 4 to 7, z = -5 to 5, and its +Y face is what touches the object. The\nfinger fits in x = -6 to 70, y = -14 to 7, z = -5 to 5. In use the pivot pin holds it and the\ndrive link pushes it: model it as the part held at both pins and squeezing with 20 N on the pad\n(the object pushes back on the pad in -Y), plus a 5 N side load along Z on the pad if the\nobject slips. Safety factor 2.5, and I'd like it under 8 g.",
